ChatGPT Intelligence Drop
=========================

Place real source material here when it should be processed on the next daily
RBB sweep rather than immediately.

Accepted formats: `.txt` and `.md`.

Deep-research cycles should write one evidence packet per run, named:

    YYYY-MM-DD_HHMM_vendor-or-scope_deep-research.md

Use `system/templates/deep_research_intelligence_drop.md` as the packet
contract. A packet may contain several observations, but every observation
must preserve its own URL, access date, evidence type, scope, confidence, and
conflicts. Never collapse a logo wall, case study, partner page, or inference
into a confirmed deployment.

Rules:

- Preserve the source text; do not save model-generated guesses as intelligence.
- Include a descriptive filename and the source URL/date inside the file when known.
- Local ChatGPT/Codex clients with workspace access may write here.
- The hosted Custom GPT cannot write local files; it must call
  `queueCaptureText` with `capture_type="deep_research"` (2026-09-19 --
  the endpoint used to hardcode `capture_type="pasted_content"`
  unconditionally, which would have mislabeled a real evidence packet;
  omitting the override no longer reproduces this folder's labeling).
- Every packet written directly to this folder must also carry a JSON
  sidecar with the same basename (`..._deep-research.json` next to the
  `..._deep-research.md`), per `system/templates/deep_research_intelligence_drop.md`.
  The sidecar is what feeds the research-quality feedback ledger in
  `system/scripts/deep_research_coverage.py` -- it records which targets the
  packet covered and which source pages were actually productive, so a
  domain that keeps producing nothing stops being re-researched. A packet
  relayed via `queueCaptureText` has no sidecar (there is nowhere local to
  put one) and is simply not scored by the feedback ledger yet.

The morning pipeline scans this folder, queues new files under
`system/captures/pending/`, and processes the pending capture queue.
Processed packets appear in the Intelligence Brief under Capture Intelligence
as `deep_research`, with the ChatGPT Intelligence Drop named as the input --
a packet relayed via `queueCaptureText` instead reports as `deep_research`
too (once the override above is passed) but under the source label "Deep
research (hosted)", not this folder's name, since it never actually landed
on disk here.
